  "limitations": [
    "Ordinary single-node profile only: one magic2 batch/partition, no idempotence, transactions, control batches, producer sequencing or LogAppendTime admission. Explicit local43/87 restrictions are distinguished from actual Apache component outcomes.",
    "Configured RF1 ISR contains only this node. acks1 and acks-1 wait for local fsync; no replicated durability, cluster quorum or production guarantee.",
    "A partition input is one atomic journal entry. A multi-partition request is not a transaction. Cancellation/timeout/shutdown during admitted sync can commit without receipt; ordinary retry can duplicate records.",
    "Trusted operator directory and exclusive process-local ownership; custom journal framing, no Apache storage format or cross-process directory lock. Historical deleted UUID files remain bounded and consume store/FD/index/disk budgets.",
    "Configured queue/result/work/index/disk/FD accounting excludes allocator bookkeeping and caller-retained outputs after transfer. Metadata/API18 direct-call concurrency remains caller-managed; transport bounds wire use.",
    "Optional pure Rust codecs normalize accepted compressed records to ordinary uncompressed magic2 with bounded workspace/work/lengths; default build rejects known compression. Zstd before Produce7 always receives76.",
    "Controlled live process restart/checkpoint and independent journal reverse decoding establish persisted data/identity behavior, not machine or power-loss injection. Physical sync-fault proofs belong to completed journal/partition/catalog cards.",
    "Official Apache serializers/parsers, ProduceRequest components and actual ordinary Java clients execute independently. Locally assembled response policy is not full Apache broker/controller runtime equivalence.",
    "Data-profile ApiVersions0-4 is independently captured and decoded; the compiled static range list alone is not a wire proof. Registry-reflected hash labels alone are not execution provenance.",
    "No Fetch/ListOffsets advertised by this source. Native Magic2 Produce remains not_run until real Fetch>=4 is implemented; no fabricated feature-negotiation range is used.",
    "No security, retention, placement, full KRaft behavior, production readiness or performance qualification. qualification remains not_run."
  ]
